Given:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The jar's volume is 10 ounces.
    \item The ingredients are salt, oil, fragrance, citrus zest, and sugar.
    \item The amount of citrus zest is the same as the amount of fragrance, so $z = f$.
    \item The amount of salt is the same as the amount of sugar, so $s = u$.
    \item The amount of oil is twice the amount of salt, so $o = 2s$.
    \item The amount of salt is twice the amount of zest, so $s = 2z$.
\end{enumerate}

The total volume of the mixture is 10 ounces, so $s + o + f + z + u = 10$.
We have $z = f$, $s = u$, $o = 2s$, and $s = 2z$.
