Let the speed of a kangaroo be $v_k$ and the distance to be traveled be $d$.
We are given that it takes 3 kangaroos traveling at the same speed $v_k$ a total of 18 hours to travel a distance $d$. So,
$3 \times v_k \times 18 = d$
$54 v_k = d$ (1)

Now we have 4 turtles, each traveling at half the speed of a kangaroo. So the speed of a turtle is $\frac{1}{2} v_k$.
Let $t$ be the number of hours it takes 4 turtles to travel the same distance $d$.
Then, $4 \times \frac{1}{2} v_k \times t = d$
$2 v_k t = d$ (2)

